# Sea Drake — an Intermediate enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 5/12 Intermediate enemies — 18 life, bribe 80 gold
# enemy: Sea Dragon — the 1997 in-game name (s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES); the deck file, s30 and the wiki call it "Sea Drake"
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0218.dck "Sea Drake (U, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 12 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 12 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/sea_drake.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 5)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/sea_drake.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Intermediate) — "Sea Dragon"
#   (Original) [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Sea Drake
22 Island
2 Island Fish Jasconius
2 Water Elemental
4 Sea Serpent
4 Siren's Call
4 Creature Bond
2 Mana Vault
4 Jump
4 Phantasmal Terrain
4 Segovian Leviathan
4 Giant Tortoise
1 Leviathan
3 Counterspell
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Counterspell
#   .vBlack  3 Counterspell
#   .vBlue   3 Counterspell
#   .vGreen  1 Lifetap, 2 Counterspell
#   .vRed    1 Blue Elemental Blast, 2 Counterspell
#   .vWhite  3 Counterspell
SB: 1 Lifetap
SB: 1 Blue Elemental Blast
